(6918965, 1043068, 81362, '<td valign="top">Lovely model and good concept for the challenge. The black triangle lower left edge distracts -- minimal doesn''t allow cropping, so in-camera quick look at all the edges becomes important (a composition skill I frequently forget, which makes me more aware of it). Could use a bit more exposure to make the whites more glaring (befitting the dramatized setting). If in an auto exposure mode (where the camera tries to make majority of picture neutral grey), exposure compensation can do that (tweak based on preview or histogram, if the camera has these features).</td>', 'Lovely model and good concept for the challenge. The black triangle lower left edge distracts -- minimal doesn''t allow cropping, so in-camera quick look at all the edges becomes important (a composition skill I frequently forget, which makes me more aware of it). Could use a bit more exposure to make the whites more glaring (befitting the dramatized setting). If in an auto exposure mode (where the camera tries to make majority of picture neutral grey), exposure compensation can do that (tweak based on preview or histogram, if the camera has these features).', '2012-12-02 08:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
