(6925810, 1043092, 68503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> What a unique sight! Congrats on your ribbon. I really wonder what that person had in mind when aligning all these plates. Any clue? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Im really not sure what his intentions were besides a small passion for expired tags. Most of the dates seem to be from the 70''s and 80''s but I found some on the back that were from the 50''s. This building is located on an old abandon farm and happened to find it a year ago on a location scouting trip. It was the first place that popped into my mind when this challenge came about.</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: What a unique sight! Congrats on your ribbon. I really wonder what that person had in mind when aligning all these plates. Any clue?   Im really not sure what his intentions were besides a small passion for expired tags. Most of the dates seem to be from the 70''s and 80''s but I found some on the back that were from the 50''s. This building is located on an old abandon farm and happened to find it a year ago on a location scouting trip. It was the first place that popped into my mind when this challenge came about.', '2012-12-07 09:54:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6925815, 1043092, 68503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by The_Tourist:</b></div><hr/><i> I think the subject (wall of a barn?) has potential for this challenge. However, I think you tried to include too much where the numbers get lost.  I think a tight composition (perhaps three plates high) would have greater impact. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I did have a shot as you suggested but I felt showing that these tags were part of a building rather than just an array would have proven better. But I will post the cropped shot later if you are interested in comparing the two. Thanks again for the comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by The_Tourist: I think the subject (wall of a barn?) has potential for this challenge. However, I think you tried to include too much where the numbers get lost.  I think a tight composition (perhaps three plates high) would have greater impact.   I did have a shot as you suggested but I felt showing that these tags were part of a building rather than just an array would have proven better. But I will post the cropped shot later if you are interested in comparing the two. Thanks again for the comments.', '2012-12-07 09:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6925816, 1043087, 146356, '<td valign="top">i m glad photographers like yourself keep pushing the bar even if sometimes the constraints push against you. <br/> <br/>I can remember times I''ve used my own poor craftsmanship as an excuse to not approach certain ideas rather than using the opportunity to better my own skills. I think works like this inspire to break out of that kind of thought-train.<br/> <br/>Great image. Love the write-ups.</td>', 'i m glad photographers like yourself keep pushing the bar even if sometimes the constraints push against you.  I can remember times I''ve used my own poor craftsmanship as an excuse to not approach certain ideas rather than using the opportunity to better my own skills. I think works like this inspire to break out of that kind of thought-train. Great image. Love the write-ups.', '2012-12-07 09:57:33.000000', NULL, 0),
